an</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><article-title>Symbiosis</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>R866</fpage><lpage>R871</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.cub.2006.09.019</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17055966</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Oliver</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Moran</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><article-title>Facultative bacterial symbionts in aphids confer resistance to parasitic wasps</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2003</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>1803</fpage><lpage>1807</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12563031</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0335320100</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hedges</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Brownlie</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Neill</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>KN</given-names></name><article-title><italic>Wolbachia </italic>and virus protection in insects</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2008</year><volume>322</volume><fpage>702</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1162418</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18974344</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Kaltenpoth</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gottler</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Herzner</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Strohm</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><article-title>Symbiotic bacteria protect wasp larvae from fung